(A value holds its own copy of what is stored in it, and a list named from
 a value holding a list is a copy too; storing a new list in one value
 leaves another named from it alone.)
a value called box is ["a"].
a list called xs is box.
append "b" to xs.
Print "box: {box}".
Print "xs: {xs}".
a value called first is ["a"].
a value called second is first.
second is ["a", "b"].
a value called third is ["x"].
a value called fourth is third.
Print "first: {first}, second: {second}".
Print "third: {third}, fourth: {fourth}".
